course: dictionary
lesson: 4147
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Glowworm can mean two different creatures, and the clues around it tell you which one is meant. Look at where the word is, what the sentence says it does, and what it looks like.
explain: In «In Waitomo Caves in New Zealand, glowworms, which are fly larvae (young flies, like maggots), glow to lure insects into sticky threads», the clues are Waitomo Caves, New Zealand, fly larvae and lure insects. So these glowworms are the young of a tiny fly, living in a cave, and their light is used as a trap.
explain: Other clues point the other way. A glowworm can be a beetle, whose female looks like a soft grub with no wings and gives off a green light from its tail at night. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does it still make sense? If the sentence talks about «glowworm caves», the glowworms are the tiny lights hanging in the dark.
fact: A glowworm is a creature that gives off light. It is a kind of beetle in one meaning, and the young of a gnat in another.
fact: In New Zealand and Australia, glowworms are tiny larvae that hang in caves and glow blue, like stars.
fact: The female beetle glowworm looks like a soft grub with no wings and gives off a green light from its tail.
fact: «Glowing like a glowworm» means shining softly in the dark.
fact: Glowworm can also be written as «glow-worm».
exercise: «In Waitomo Caves in New Zealand, glowworms, which are fly larvae, glow to lure insects into sticky threads.» What are these glowworms? | A kind of beetle with wings | A kind of star in the sky | *The young of a fly, called larvae | A bird that sings at night
exercise: The female beetle glowworm looks like what? | *A soft grub with no wings | A shiny green stone | A glass bottle | A tiny bird
exercise: Ella says, «The cave was lit by glowworms, like a starry sky.» What does «glowing like a glowworm» suggest? | *Shining softly in the dark | Very cold and wet | Running very fast | Hidden under a rock
test: «The glowworms lit the cave ceiling like stars.» What does lit mean here? | Cleaned | Hid | Dropped | *Made bright with light
test: Why do the glowworm larvae in Waitomo Caves glow? | To sing to other glowworms | To keep warm in the cold | To hide from the sun | *To lure insects into sticky threads
exam: Which word in «glowworms, which are fly larvae (young flies, like maggots)» tells you the glowworms are still young? | Threads | *Larvae | Glow | Caves
